The reviewers broadly agree that the problem of molecular structure elucidation from IR spectra is interesting, and that the proposed multi-agent framework is reasonable. The main concerns are:
(1) Low absolute performance and the inherent ambiguity of IR-only structure elucidation;
(2) Insufficient evaluation in the initial submission;
(3) Depth and novelty of the agentic design;
(4) Unclear scope and robustness, including sensitivity to the translator, retrieval database coverage, and handling of mixtures.
